# M39 (PLAN_BROWSER_PERF_SECURITY.md §2.10, D49) — isolated POST-only rung on the echo-server
# harness: a single static (non-interpolated, no capture) POST with body, split out of bench.tflw's
# combined GET+POST shape. Mirrors M34's own isolation logic (a static POST body, no capture chain)
# so this rung measures tflw's raw POST-with-body overhead alone, not entangled with a preceding
# GET or a captured/interpolated field.

test "M39 echo POST-only"
  ramp to 30 users over 8s
  api POST /orders body { items: [{ productId: "prod_1", quantity: 1 }] }
  expect status equals 201
  # `TF033` (tflw M60): a workload-bearing test's verdict comes only from its thresholds, so one is
  # required. This rung measures rather than gates, so the bound is deliberately loose — but not
  # vacuous: echo-server.mjs is a zero-latency local process with nothing to contend over, so any
  # error at all is a defect in the harness or the generator. See perf/README.md for how this ladder
  # is run and checked.
  threshold error rate is less than 1%
